# s17_if_reject.tkr — §17 `#if` region reject host. Three malformed regions live one per namespace
# under src/, and the single failing build reports every diagnostic it finds, one per scenario below:
# an unterminated region, an `#elseif` after `#else`, and an empty `#if()` predicate.

Feature: §17 #if region reject — the compiler rejects malformed conditional-compilation regions

  Scenario: unterminated — a `#if` region with no `#endif` is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "unterminated `#if` region (expected `#endif`)"

  Scenario: else_order — an `#elseif` after `#else` is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "`#elseif` may not follow `#else` in a `#if` region"

  Scenario: empty_pred — a `#if()` with no predicate is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "expected a predicate"
